# Flink Gzipped CSV Source Parsing

## Purpose
Read gzipped CSV files in Flink, parse rows with missing fields, and map to POJO types.

## Reading `.gz` as Text
Flink's `readTextFile` and `TextInputFormat` support gzip files automatically.
```java
DataStream<String> lines = env.readTextFile(taskInputPath);
```

## Robust CSV Split
Use `split(",", -1)` to preserve empty fields.
```java
String[] parts = line.split(",", -1);
```

## Minimal Parsing Pattern
```java
DataStream<MyEvent> events = lines.flatMap((String line, Collector<MyEvent> out) -> {
  String[] p = line.split(",", -1);
  if (p.length < 6) return; // skip bad lines
  long timestampMicros = Long.parseLong(p[0]);
  long jobId = Long.parseLong(p[2]);
  int eventType = Integer.parseInt(p[5]);
  out.collect(new MyEvent(timestampMicros / 1000L, jobId, eventType));
}).returns(MyEvent.class);
